    <string name="wf_bridge_title">3. Sony FX3 camera</string>
    <string name="wf_bridge_offline">Windows bridge not connected</string>
    <string name="wf_bridge_explain">Live camera control runs through the Windows program and the Sony Camera Remote SDK in slice 3. For now, record on the camera itself and log each take here.</string>
    <string name="wf_fix_title">When an error appears: cause and fix</string>
    <string name="wf_fix1_err">The PC does not see the camera</string>
    <string name="wf_fix1_do">On the camera: Menu → Network → PC Remote = On, connection method = USB. Use a data USB-C cable plugged straight into the PC, no hub.</string>
    <string name="wf_fix2_err">The connection drops</string>
    <string name="wf_fix2_do">Close Imaging Edge and any other app using the camera, and turn off USB power saving in Windows.</string>
    <string name="wf_fix3_err">Recording does not start</string>
    <string name="wf_fix3_do">Check that a memory card with free space is inserted and the camera is not in playback mode.</string>
    <string name="wf_fix4_err">The software refuses the camera</string>
    <string name="wf_fix4_do">FX3 firmware must be 2.00 or later. Update it from Sony\'s website.</string>
    <string name="wf_fix5_err">Overheating warning</string>
    <string name="wf_fix5_do">Set Auto Power OFF Temp to High, keep the camera out of direct light and leave room for airflow.</string>
    <string name="wf_tips_title">Distance, lighting and direction tips</string>
    <string name="wf_tip_distance">Stand about 1.5–2 m in front of the green screen to reduce shadows and green spill.</string>
    <string name="wf_tip_frame">In the vertical frame put the eyes on the upper third with little headroom. Move closer for a close-up, farther for a medium shot.</string>
    <string name="wf_tip_light">Place the NEEWER light at about 45° to the side, slightly above eye level. If the face is too bright, dim it or move it back.</string>
    <string name="wf_tip_shadow">If your shadow appears on the background, step away from it.</string>
    <string name="wf_tip_angle">For narration: camera at eye level. For dramatic scenes: change the angle or movement as suggested per scene below.</string>
    <string name="wf_tip_approx">Distances are approximate. Live measurement from the camera image comes in slice 4.</string>
    <string name="wf_scene_not_analysed">This scene has not been analysed yet (step 2).</string>
